    "_sourceUrl": "https://hsds.ac.uk/data-catalogue/resource/7a38e34a150d1cbd8b7b44284345dc276dbe7540a2e80b2a3184e9114a47dfc7",
    "title": "Radiocarbon date, Sample number OxA-819",
    "description": "Bone, id as human femur by C L Royle, sample 1718 from one of second period of 14 flat-grave inhumations, context 2001 (body stain) within context 2008 (grave fill) in Feature 109 (grave cut) at Sutton Hoo, Woodbridge, Suffolk, England. Comment (subm P B): No datable finds have been recovered from the very degraded burials immediately east of the mounds, so this date is of particular importance, relating the flat-grave cemetery to the c AD 625 ship burial. Comment (lab): calibrated mean (on Stuiver-Pearson 1986 curve) for the date is cal AD 811, 847, 851; at two sds the range is c AD 665-985.<br>Flat inhumation cemetery beyond mounds",
    "creator": "M O H Carver & P Bethell (Sutton Hoo Res Trust) 1984/5",
